s accompanying under Tang Wei's own authority. Other Qin forces on the campaign roster: 73,200 troops in 3 formation(s), under Kanki, Mou Gou, Ousen, at Qin Capital Basin, Qin Northern Frontier, task: concentrate Mou Gou, Ousen, and Kanki field forces for the northern Wei campaign; 46,100 troops in 2 formation(s), under Ouki, Tou, at Qin Eastern March, task: concentrate Ouki and Tou field forces for the northern Wei campaign; 40,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Mou Bu, at Qin Southern March, task: hold Mou Bu's shock army ready for the northern Wei campaign; 5,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Fan Yi, at Qin Capital Basin, task: maintain the Qin mobile reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign; 3,000 troops in 1 formation(s), under Shou Hei Kun, at Qin Eastern Military Depot, task: maintain the eastern reserve as a participant in the northern Wei campaign. Combined Qin strength on the current campaign roster is 176,800. The staff designate Kanyou as the present operational area. The field command has completed its lawful staging at Kanyou; Sanyou remains the strategic target, but Qin has not yet authorized entry into Wei territory. Intelligence estimate: an official estimate of roughly 94,000-156,000 troops able to influence the theater; reported opposing commanders: Deng Shan, Gai Mou, Go Hou Mei, Huan Zhen, Jing Ning, Jing Rong, Luo Qian, Qiao He, Qiao Jie, Rei Ou; no confirmed battle contact. These are staff estimates rather than confirmed enemy counts. The Bureau's standing orders record concentration at Kanyou as complete. Further advance into Wei territory awaits new lawful entry authority.","confidence_milli":800,"information_ref":"information.qin_campaign_briefing.a98b9575d13e9931a873","learned_at":"244-BCE-09-16T20:22:48+08:00","provenance":"Qin Military Bureau operational briefing","source_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign","subject_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign"},{"claim":"Field-command arrival report: Tang Wei's field army has reached Sanyou and completed the current concentration/advance phase. March security placed the army's assigned forward-security element on forward security/reconnaissance. Current staff intelligence remains roughly 94,000-156,000 troops able to influence the theater; no confirmed battle contact. The army has not been committed to a battle or further advance by this report. The command remains ready for a follow-on order, confirmed enemy contact, or Tang Wei's own lawful reconnaissance and maneuver decisions.","confidence_milli":700,"information_ref":"information.campaign_phase.4e0077add2f9b0df46dc","learned_at":"244-BCE-09-23T05:22:48+08:00","provenance":"field-command staff report","source_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign","subject_ref":"arc_ryo_fui_northern_wei_campaign"},{"claim":"Forward reconnaissance in Wei Western Corridor confirms 8 enemy formations, approximately 41,500 troops in observed strength. The patrol identifies 10 usable mapped approach routes touching the assigned area. This confirms observed presence only; it does not establish enemy intent, future movement, or initiate battle.","confidence_milli":746,"information_ref":"information.military_reconnaissance.c94ea53daeb7008e6cb4","learned_at":"244-BCE-09-28T05:00:00+08:00","provenance":"military_reconnaissance","source_ref":"char_ren_qiao","subject_ref":"military_reconnaissance:loc_wei_regional_02"}],"information_refs":["information.qin_campaign_briefing.a98b9575d13e9931a873","information.campaign_phase.4e0077add2f9b0df46dc","information.military_reconnaissance.c94ea53daeb7008e6cb4"],"phase":"material_intelligence","report_ref":"campaign_command_material_report.3caf6ca538955d60526e","reported_at":"244-BCE-09-29T18:00:00+08:00","to_ref":"char_mou_gou"},{"directive_ref":"campaign_directive_9366b39316b6a2913d9e","event_ref":"event_campaign_command_dawn_74f262cf7c2a54cdf9df","from_ref":"char_tang_wei","locations":{"loc_sanyou":9500},"order_ref":"operational_order_b428477bcff3f7cc52d5","per